  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or slightly negative (≤ 0.00) and historical price trend shows mean reversion.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes by applying a 10-15% dampening factor to the immediate next period.",
    "When sentiment is positive (≥ 0.50), increase forecast volatility but cap upward bias at +5% above recent 7-day average to avoid overcorrection.",
    "If model consistently overpredicts early in the 30-day horizon, shift forecast peak to later days (e.g., delay by 2-3 days) to align with observed lagged behavior.",
    "Apply downward bias correction if true outcome is consistently below 3-day moving average of model forecast — especially when sentiment is flat or negative."
